title: 'One constraint lies under all seven: one person''s attention.'
pid: 0a3b54bb-3463-4ccb-90e6-db1554b1bd50
body: |2-
  This reading is mine. Jeff has not said it in these words.
  Jeff holds that [[id:0c399e74-6d5e-4f0a-95e5-331a7239b19d][elegance is constrained optimization]].
  Here the constraint is that he is the only human. He reads
  the code, the plans and the reviews, and many agents write them.
  So the expensive thing is whatever costs him a second reading,
  a question, or a round of review. Tokens are cheap beside it.
  Principles 1, 2, 3, 4 and 7 spend his attention well.
  Principles 5 and 6 keep his data and his decisions from being
  spent without him.
